1
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,000
He's a jew. He’s a Neo-Nazi. With one true enemy… Himself!

2
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:26,000
The Believer is a drama film directed by Henry Bean.

3
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:06,000
A hardcore US racist skinhead who, because of his intelligence, leads a gang dedicated to
fighting the enemy: the supposed American-Jewish conspiracy for domination.

4
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:46,000
However, he's hiding a secret: he's Jewish-born, a brilliant scholar whose questioning of the tenets of his faith has
left him angry and confused, turning against those who he thinks have a tragic history of their own making.

5
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Danny Balint, played by Ryan Gosling.

6
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Carla Moebius, played by Summer Phoenix.

7
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Lina Moebius, played by Theresa Russell.

8
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Curtis Zampf, played by Billy Zane.

9
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Billings, played by Garret Dillahunt.

10
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Guy Danielsen, played by A.D. Miles.

11
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
The Believer is a 2001 American drama film written and directed by Henry Bean in his
feature directorial debut, based on a story by Bean and Mark Jacobson.

12
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Starring Ryan Gosling, Billy Zane, Theresa Russell, and Summer Phoenix, the
film follows Daniel Balint, a Jew who becomes a neo-Nazi.

13
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
The film is loosely based on the true story of Dan Burros, a member of the American Nazi Party and the New York branch of the
United Klans of America who died by suicide after being revealed as Jewish by a reporter from The New York Times.

14
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
The Believer premiered at the Sundance Film Festival on January
19, 2001, where it won the Grand Jury Prize.

15
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
It was theatrically released in the United States on May 17, 2002, to
positive reviews, with particular praise for Gosling's performance.

16
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
The film earned several accolades, including the Golden St.

17
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
George at the 23rd Moscow International Film Festival.

18
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
It received four nominations at the 17th Independent Spirit Awards, Best First Feature and Best
Screenplay for Bean, Best Male Lead for Gosling, and Best Supporting Female for Summer Phoenix.

19
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
The film explores themes of new york city,
neo-nazism, antisemitism, bigotry, hatred.

20
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
The tone is emotional.
